+└──────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────────┴──────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
+
+How they connect: the website POSTs appearance settings to the backend; the backend persists them (MariaDB) and renders fields/uniforms/plays as PNG/GIF. The ref bot calls backend game
+endpoints. This is a college-football-sim ("FCFB") platform; "arceus" is the ba
+
+FCFB-Backend active branch: add-animations-to-plays. fcfb-website active branchNothing from this work is committed (the owner, Andrew, commits everythinghimself — never run git commit/push/tag, and never add AI attribution anywhere).
+
+Build / verify (run before considering any change done)
+
+Backend (JDKs via jenv; this project needs a modern JDK pinned via the toolchain):
+cd /Users/apkick/Programming/FCFB-Backend
+./gradlew compileKotlin ktlintMainSourceSetCheck -Dorg.gradle.jvmargs="-Xmx2g"
+./gradlew test --tests "*Field*" --tests "*Appearance*" --tests "*Bowl*" --tests "*Postseason*" -Dorg.gradle.jvmargs="-Xmx2g"
+- Always pass -Dorg.gradle.jvmargs="-Xmx2g" or the Kotlin compile daemon OOMs ("GC overhead limit exceeded"); if it hangs, ./gradlew --stop first.
+- Tests run on H2 with spring.flyway.enabled=false, so migrations do not apply during tests. ktlint: max line length 140, argument-list-wrapping enforced; ./gradlew ktlintMainSourceSetFormat auto-fixes most wrapping/import-order issues.
+- To visually verify a render, write a throwaway JUnit test under src/test/kotl/fcfb/animation/ that calls FieldBackgroundPainter.paint(theme) (overhead) orGoalPostScenePainter.paint(...) (field-goal scene) and ImageIO.writes a PNG to /private/tmp/claude-501/, then read the PNG. Delete the throwaway test after (FieldTheme/Team/TeamField are easy to construct in-memory).
+
+Website:
+cd /Users/apkick/Programming/fcfb-website
+npm run lint          # eslint src --ext .js,.jsx   (lint:fix to auto-fix)
+There's no backend-independent visual harness for the React editor; layout must be eyeballed in a running app (npm run start).
+
+Backend architecture you'll need
+
+Field appearance is split across three JPA base types → five physical tables:
+- @MappedSuperclass FieldAppearance → TeamField (team_field) + GameField (game_napshot). File: model/FieldAppearance.kt (note its copyAppearanceInto(target) —any new column must be copied there too).
+- @MappedSuperclass PostseasonField → PlayoffField (playoff_field) + ConferenceChampionshipField (conference_championship_field). File: model/PostseasonField.kt (also has a
+  copyAppearanceInto-style copy).
+- BowlField (bowl_field) — standalone. File: model/BowlField.kt (also has a copy method).
+
+So a new field-appearance column added "everywhere" means: add the property to those three model files (+ each copy method), add the ALTER TABLE to all 5 tables in one migration, add it to the three request DTOs and their three appliers, and resolve it in FieldTheme.
+
+Uniforms live on TeamUniformCurrent (team_uniform_current, what the editor edit(team_uniform_history, a per-week game snapshot written by TeamUniformService).A new uniform column must be added in four places: both model files, the TeamUniformHistory positional secondary constructor, and the TeamUniformService snapshot call.
+
+Key files:
+- Painters: service/fcfb/animation/FieldBackgroundPainter.kt (overhead field), GoalPostScenePainter.kt (field-goal 3D-ish scene), FieldGoalPlayerPainter.kt (field-goal player figures), HelmetSprite.kt (detailed side helmet, marker-recolor: red=facemask, green=stripe, white=shell), Uniforms.kt (builds home/away Uniforms, forMatchup).
+- Theme: FieldTheme.kt (resolves every field setting; yardNumberOutlineScale(),c.), FieldThemeResolver.kt (chooses team vs game-field vs bowl vs postseason).
+- Services: TeamAppearanceService (controller→service entry for team edits), FieldAppearanceApplier (team field request→entity), BowlFieldService, PostseasonFieldUpdater, AppearancePreviewService + AppearanceThumbnailCache (cached grid thumbnails).
+- DTOs: dto/request/{TeamFieldRequest,BowlFieldRequest,PostseasonFieldRequest,TeamUniformRequest}.kt.
+- Migrations: src/main/resources/db/migration/ (current max is V51). Font assets: src/main/resources/*.otf.
+- Fonts: EndZoneFonts.kt (font-value encoding; a value is KEY or KEY|BOLD via BOLD_SUFFIX; familyOf strips the suffix, styleFor returns BOLD only if present — default is natural weight), NumberFonts.kt, FontRegistry.kt, FontService.kt.
+
+Website appearance UI:
+- src/components/team/appearance/ — AppearanceEditor.jsx (the generic renderer:fit, minmax(220px,1fr)) grid; supports field types incl. subheading, divider,and fullWidth/rowSpan cell hints), appearanceSections.js (team field/uniform/color section definitions + formFrom/payloadFrom), appearanceForm.js (readGeneric/writeGeneric), FontControl.jsx, AppearanceControl.jsx.
+- src/components/admin/fieldAppearance/fieldDefinitions.js — bowl/playoff/CCG fOWL_SECTIONS, CCG_SECTIONS, PLAYOFF_SECTIONS, NC_SECTIONS).
+- Field types used: color/optionalColor/colorToken, toggle (often transient + derivedFrom), select, font, scale (slider multiplier, fallback:1), graphic, stripe, logo, subheading, divider.
+
+🚨 Deploy/boot blockers (unresolved)
+
+1. V37 Flyway checksum mismatch. The shared dev MariaDB (jdbc:mariadb://51.81.32.234/arceus) already has V37 applied with an old checksum, so a real backend boot fails. Fix on the dev
+   DB: delete the flyway_schema_history rows for the affected versions and DROPady-added appearance columns, then restart so current migrations re-apply. Never edit an applied migration file to fix this — add a new DROP COLUMN IF EXISTS migration instead (editing V41 previously caused exactly this trap). Prod is unaffected (these are "future" migrations, ignored there via ignoreFutureMigrations).
+2. BOT_SERVICE_KEY service auth. The backend's ref-bot endpoints were hardened to require a service key. You must set BOT_SERVICE_KEY in Jenkins and update FCFB-Discord-Ref-Bot to send header X-Service-Key: <BOT_SERVICE_KEY> on its backend calls, or the bot's requests get rejected. This is the main outstanding ref-bot item.
+
+Migrations added on this branch (V37 → V51)
+
+One Flyway version per batch; immutable once applied anywhere. Recent: V48 away pants, V49 yard-number direction-arrow align, V50 conference-logo size (the 25s), V51 outline widths (yard number / end zone / wall text). Full per-migration notes are in persistent memory at …/memory/appearance_migrations_pending.md.
+
+Done this session (all green, uncommitted)
+
+Rendering (backend): triple-stripe flush-vs-gap variant + thinner single stripeiangles (overhead + field-goal, point toward the near end zone;Center/Top/Bottom align, default Top; size/gap/inset tuned; gap widens when the number is outlined); top-row yard numbers flipped 180° to read from the top sideline (arrow stays pointing at the goal); away pants on the road uniform; conference-logo size on the 25s; outline-width multipliers (yard number/end zone/wall). Also removed over-explaining KDoc comments.
+
+Editor (website): postseason-appearance URL routing + team-appearance tab-in-URL; per-font-selector Bold checkbox (default natural weight); facemask white-pixel fix; Jersey section
+split Home/Away; Markings section rebuilt — outline-color + font cells row-spanntrol tucks under the outline toggle, and red-zone / midfield / sideline eachsit on their own row separated by horizontal dividers (new divider field type + rowSpan support added to AppearanceEditor.jsx).
